<title>UK: Shares in Life Sciences jump on agreed bid.</title>
<headline>Shares in Life Sciences jump on agreed bid.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in scientific equipment maker Life Sciences International Plc were indicated sharply higher on Tuesday after news of an agreed bid for the company from Thermo Instrument Systems Inc of the U.S.</p>
<p>The shares leapt 40p to 132-1/2p by 0818 GMT in pre-market trade.</p>
<p>The U.S. group made a 135p per share agreed cash offer for the British group, valuing the latter at around 235.9 million stg.</p>
<p>--Elaine Hardcastle, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
</text>
